                        <p>Hair is an important aspect of your appearance and hair loss can affect your confidence and self-esteem. Hair loss problem has been affecting more than 40% of the population. Male pattern baldness is very common and lots of men are looking for various surgical and non-surgical solutions for the same.</p>
                        <p>While there are many treatments promoted for male pattern hair loss including simple non-invasive laser therapy, PRP therapy, FDA-approved drugs or others; these treatments may give some temporary relief or slow down the hair fall process however, hair transplantation remains the only proven, and permanent solution.</p>

                        <h3 class="blog_heading">Is it permanent?</h3>
                        <p><a href="https://www.iconiquebydrbkgarg.com/Is-hair-transplant-a-safe">Is hair transplant safe</a> and permanent or? Those who are considering the hair transplant option often worry about this. The good news is that hair transplantation is known for its permanent and natural effects. Hair loss is mainly associated with the hormone dihydrotestosterone (DHT) that causes hair to fall. During hair transplantation, the newly transplanted hair grows irrespective of the effect of DHT. Thus, this new hair continues to grow and offer a permanent solution. You can see the new hair come through as early as 4 to 5 months after the procedure, you can see and enjoy the fuller look and permanent effects of the transplanted hair in about 10-12 months. These transplanted hairs continue to grow for the rest of your life.</p>
                        <p>Is the procedure safe? Most people want to know whether the treatment is safe and what are the side effects. In simple words, the hair transplantation treatment is safe and has a good success rate. The procedure is done by hair experts with excellent knowledge and effective tools to make the procedure safer. By choosing the right clinic, and the right surgeon to conduct the procedure, you can minimize the risks and complications.</p>

                        <h3 class="blog_heading">Types of procedures</h3>
                        <p>There are two types of procedures: FUE and FUT. FUE Technique (Follicular Unit Extraction) involves harvesting the grafts or follicles one by one from the donor area at the back of the head. FUT, Follicular Unit Transplantation, is the conventional method, also called the strip method, wherein the hair specialist takes a strip of hair-bearing skin from the back of the scalp.</p>
                        <p>FUE is a less invasive technique and there is minimum scarring involved. After transplantation is complete, there are no requirements of stitches and it will only leave small, practically invisible scars. While in FUT a large cut is taken and requires more time to recover. The pain experienced after surgery also varies according to the technique used.</p>
                        <p>Both these methods are safe and are done by experts in hair transplantation.</p>
                        <p>The choice of procedure is based on availability of donor hair and balding patterns. FUE can be particularly suitable for patients with less donor hair available on the head and who wants to use body hair.</p>
                        <p>Both these procedures have been used in the hair industry for years and with recent innovations with respect to equipment and techniques, such as the introduction of a robotic system for harvesting grafts makes the process safer with little or no side effects.</p>
                        <p>The most assured way to get the successful outcome is to choose the right hair professional to perform the procedure.</p>

                        <h3 class="blog_heading">Is it possible that you could need another hair transplant?</h3>
                        <p>If you are going under a hair transplant, you must be worrying if a single procedure is enough or do another procedure in the future. In most cases, a single surgery is sufficient to achieve the desired results. If you are suffering from mild to moderate hair loss pattern and slightly receding hairline, then a single hair transplant is sufficient to cover the balding area. In a few cases, people continue to suffer from hair loss and new balding spots start to appear again. This is common for people having extensive or an advanced form of hair loss condition and they may require an additional procedure to fill in the new balding area.</p>

                        <h3 class="blog_heading">Results</h3>
                        <p>People suffer from different types of hair loss patterns. Hair transplantation is particularly suitable for lowering an inherited high hairline. FUE technique is an excellent way to treat hair thinning appearance. Both FUT and FUE can be used to successfully cover scars around the hairline in both men and women. The natural-looking results are depending upon the skills of the surgeon, type of hair loss, availability of donor’s hair, etc. When performed by the expert surgeon, hair transplantation delivers results so natural in appearance, no one will notice the difference between natural and transplanted hair.</p>
                        <p>The surgeons use state-of-the-art instruments and select the finer hair for the hairline and thicker grafts for added density. With careful selection and planting at the right angle, a more youthful and natural hairline can be created. This is also depending upon the meticulous and artistic work done by the hair specialist. For achieving the best results ensure that the surgeon has an excellent track record and relevant experience, advanced technique and technology are used and the clinic has a high success rate.</p>

                        <h3 class="blog_heading">What to expect long-term</h3>
                        <p>Post-surgery, it is common to shred a few hairs. The newly transplanted hair grows at the rate of 0.5 to 1 cm per month and one can see the visible results in 8 to 12 months.</p>
                        <p>If you are prone to further thinning or hair loss then you can consult the specialist for any hair fall control medications. This will lessen your chance of further hair loss and the new hair continues to grow to give you a fuller, natural look. In a few cases, one may require additional surgery to cover the balding area caused due to further hair loss problems.</p>
                        <p>The replanted hair is permanent and one can treat them as natural hair, straighten them, curl them, color them, and style them as per one wish.</p>

                        <h3 class="blog_heading">When to talk to a doctor</h3>
                        <p>Everyone shreds a few hairs every day but if you are losing more than 50 hairs per day, if you are noticing drastic hair thinning and balding areas, it is time to visit the doctor. The qualified hair expert will evaluate your situation, conduct a detailed assessment, and advise you about the most suitable transplant procedure. He/she can also advise you on how to arrest further loss.</p>

                        <h3 class="blog_heading">The bottom line</h3>
                        <p>Hair transplantation is a proven, safe and permanent method of hair restoration with permanent results and FUE is the most advanced technique to achieve the most natural-looking results. With the FUE technique, you will receive permanent results with minimal scarring and minimal discomfort. The latest innovations in the field and cutting edge technologies have drastically increased the success rate of the procedure. It’s not just hair you restore but it’s your chance to regain your confidence too. Visit the most experienced team to transform your appearance and your life.</p>
